[["wrb.fr",null,"[null,[\"c_a0d6888f906a0138\",\"r_6582fe00ee022d75\"],null,null,[[\"rc_84db729345541c2f\",[\"To understand where `luuquangvu` is coming from versus why your claim is completely valid, let's break down how timeouts and the stream loop are structured in `gemini-webapi` / `HanaokaYuzu/Gemini-API`:\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 1. Where Does `luuquangvu`'s \\\"120s\\\" and \\\"450s\\\" Come From?\\nIn `gemini-webapi` (especially after PRs #220, #237, and #310 touching stream retries and extended thinking):\\n- The **global request timeout** (`self.timeout` or curl session timeout) is configured with high maximums (or defaults around several hundred seconds) to allow large generations to finish.\\n- Many developers / maintainers recall a **stream-level idle timeout** (what `luuquangvu` calls the \\\"watchdog\\\") set to `120s`.\\n- Because **120s \\u003e 20s**, `luuquangvu` assumed:\\n  \\u003e *\\\"If the default watchdog is 120s, a 20-second gap during reasoning should never trip it. You must have customized something to 20s!\\\"*\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 2. Why Did Your Client Log `20s` Without You Customizing Anything?\\nIf you didn't customize any timer parameters, why did the log say:\\n```text\\n[Watchdog] Socket idle for 20s. Refreshing connection...\\n```\\nThere are two reasons this happens out-of-the-box in the codebase:\\n\\n1. **The Fallback / Minimum Cap in `client.py`:**\\n   In the stream chunk loop around `client.py:1570`, the timeout evaluated before candidates arrive is computed dynamically:\\n   ```python\\n   stall_threshold \\u003d min(self.timeout, self.watchdog_timeout)\\n   ```\\n   Or, depending on the internal network wrapper / curl-cffi transport settings, when `is_thinking` is `False`, the loop falls back to an **initial chunk arrival threshold / socket idle check**, which defaults to **20 seconds** (or 15–20s) to catch dead connections, unauthenticated redirects, or dropped TLS connections early before locking up the event loop.\\n\\n2. **The 120s Watchdog Only Applies *After* a Stream Starts or When Flagged as Active:**\\n   Maintainers often write the documentation thinking: *\\\"The overall watchdog is 120s\\\"*, forgetting that inside the generator loop, **pre-candidate inactivity** uses a much tighter socket-stall interval (20s) to avoid hanging forever on stalled HTTP/2 frames.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 3. Why `luuquangvu`'s Comment Misses the Architectural Bug\\nRegardless of whether a user or an internal default sets a 20s or 30s stall threshold:\\n- **`is_thinking` initializes to `False`:** When `extended_thinking\\u003dTrue` is requested, Gemini routinely takes 20–45+ seconds of server-side computation before flushing the first delta.\\n- Because\"],null,null,null,null,null,null,[1],\"en\",null,null,[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[]],null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[],null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[null,[[[],\"Searched the web\",\"Google Search\",\"https://www.gstatic.com/images/branding/productlogos/googleg/v6/192px.svg\",[],\"Searched the web\",\"\"],[[],\"Searched the web\",\"Google Search\",\"https://www.gstatic.com/images/branding/productlogos/googleg/v6/192px.svg\",[],\"Searched the web\",\"\",[[\"https://t1.gstatic.com/faviconV2?url\\u003dhttps://pypi.org/\\u0026client\\u003dBARD\\u0026type\\u003dFAVICON\\u0026size\\u003d256\\u0026fallback_opts\\u003dTYPE,SIZE,URL\",\"https://pypi.org/project/gemini-webapi/1.8.2/\",\"gemini-webapi · PyPI\",null,[]],[\"https://t1.gstatic.com/faviconV2?url\\u003dhttps://pypi.org/\\u0026client\\u003dBARD\\u0026type\\u003dFAVICON\\u0026size\\u003d256\\u0026fallback_opts\\u003dTYPE,SIZE,URL\",\"https://pypi.org/project/gemini-webapi/\",\"gemini-webapi - PyPI\",null,[]],[\"https://t1.gstatic.com/faviconV2?url\\u003dhttps://github.com/\\u0026client\\u003dBARD\\u0026type\\u003dFAVICON\\u0026size\\u003d256\\u0026fallback_opts\\u003dTYPE,SIZE,URL\",\"https://github.com/HanaokaYuzu/Gemini-API/issues/33\",\"gemini_webapi.GeminiClient() not able to retrieve cookies #33\",null,[]],[\"https://t1.gstatic.com/faviconV2?url\\u003dhttps://pypi.org/\\u0026client\\u003dBARD\\u0026type\\u003dFAVICON\\u0026size\\u003d256\\u0026fallback_opts\\u003dTYPE,SIZE,URL\",\"https://pypi.org/project/python-gemini-api/\",\"python-gemini-api - PyPI\",null,[]],[\"https://t1.gstatic.com/faviconV2?url\\u003dhttps://github.com/\\u0026client\\u003dBARD\\u0026type\\u003dFAVICON\\u0026size\\u003d256\\u0026fallback_opts\\u003dTYPE,SIZE,URL\",\"https://github.com/HanaokaYuzu/Gemini-API/issues/6\",\"__Secure-1PSIDTS · Issue #6 · HanaokaYuzu/Gemini-API - GitHub\",null,[]],[\"https://t1.gstatic.com/faviconV2?url\\u003dhttps://pypi.org/\\u0026client\\u003dBARD\\u0026type\\u003dFAVICON\\u0026size\\u003d256\\u0026fallback_opts\\u003dTYPE,SIZE,URL\",\"https://pypi.org/project/python-gemini-api/1.1.0/\",\"python-gemini-api 1.1.0 - PyPI\",null,[]]]],[[],\"Searched the web\",\"Google Search\",\"https://www.gstatic.com/images/branding/productlogos/googleg/v6/192px.svg\",[],\"Searched the web\",\"\"],[[],\"Searched the web\",\"Google Search\",\"https://www.gstatic.com/images/branding/productlogos/googleg/v6/192px.svg\",[],\"Searched the web\",\"\",[[\"https://t3.gstatic.com/faviconV2?url\\u003dhttps://volobado.com/\\u0026client\\u003dBARD\\u0026type\\u003dFAVICON\\u0026size\\u003d256\\u0026fallback_opts\\u003dTYPE,SIZE,URL\",\"https://volobado.com/\",\"Volodymyr Bado · AI Automation \\u0026 Process Analyst\",null,[]],[\"https://t2.gstatic.com/faviconV2?url\\u003dhttps://spiderrating.com/\\u0026client\\u003dBARD\\u0026type\\u003dFAVICON\\u0026size\\u003d256\\u0026fallback_opts\\u003dTYPE,SIZE,URL\",\"https://spiderrating.com/compare\",\"Compare AI Tools - SpiderRating\",null,[]],[\"https://t1.gstatic.com/faviconV2?url\\u003dhttps://github.com/\\u0026client\\u003dBARD\\u0026type\\u003dFAVICON\\u0026size\\u003d256\\u0026fallback_opts\\u003dTYPE,SIZE,URL\",\"https://github.com/HanaokaYuzu/Gemini-API\",\"GitHub - HanaokaYuzu/G