aYuzu/Gemini-API:\",[[20,30,[[null,null,null,null,3]]],[157,170,[[null,null,null,null,3]]],[173,195,[[null,null,null,null,3]]]]]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[]],[null,[null,3,\"1. Where Does luuquangvu's \\\"120s\\\" and \\\"450s\\\" Come From?\",[[14,24,[[null,null,null,null,3]]]]]],[null,[null,0,\"In gemini-webapi (especially after PRs #220, #237, and #310 touching stream retries and extended thinking):\",[[3,16,[[null,null,null,null,3]]]]]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[[[[[null,[null,0,\"The global request timeout (self.timeout or curl session timeout) is configured with high maximums (or defaults around several hundred seconds) to allow large generations to finish.\",[[4,26,[[null,null,null,null,2]]],[28,40,[[null,null,null,null,3]]]]]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"Many developers / maintainers recall a stream-level idle timeout (what luuquangvu calls the \\\"watchdog\\\") set to 120s.\",[[39,64,[[null,null,null,null,2]]],[71,81,[[null,null,null,null,3]]],[111,115,[[null,null,null,null,3]]]]]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"Because 120s \\u003e 20s, luuquangvu assumed:\",[[8,18,[[null,null,null,null,2]]],[20,30,[[null,null,null,null,3]]]]]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[[[null,[null,0,\"\\\"If the default watchdog is 120s, a 20-second gap during reasoning should never trip it. You must have customized something to 20s!\\\"\",[[0,132,[[null,null,null,null,1]]]]]]]]]]]]]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[]],[null,[null,3,\"2. Why Did Your Client Log 20s Without You Customizing Anything?\",[[27,30,[[null,null,null,null,3]]]]]],[null,[null,0,\"If you didn't customize any timer parameters, why did the log say:\"]],[null,null,null,[\"[Watchdog] Socket idle for 20s. Refreshing connection...\\n\",\"text\"]],[null,[null,0,\"There are two reasons this happens out-of-the-box in the c