ox in the codebase:\"]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[[[[[null,[null,0,\"The Fallback / Minimum Cap in client.py:\\nIn the stream chunk loop around client.py:1570, the timeout evaluated before candidates arrive is computed dynamically:\",[[30,39,[[null,null,null,null,3]]],[0,40,[[null,null,null,null,2]]],[73,87,[[null,null,null,null,3]]]]]],[null,null,null,[\"stall_threshold \\u003d min(self.timeout, self.watchdog_timeout)\\n\",\"python\"]],[null,[null,0,\"Or, depending on the internal network wrapper / curl-cffi transport settings, when is_thinking is False, the loop falls back to an initial chunk arrival threshold / socket idle check, which defaults to 20 seconds (or 15–20s) to catch dead connections, unauthenticated redirects, or dropped TLS connections early before locking up the event loop.\",[[83,94,[[null,null,null,null,3]]],[98,103,[[null,null,null,null,3]]],[131,182,[[null,null,null,null,2]]],[202,212,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"The 120s Watchdog Only Applies After a Stream Starts or When Flagged as Active:\\nMaintainers often write the documentation thinking: \\\"The overall watchdog is 120s\\\", forgetting that inside the generator loop, pre-candidate inactivity uses a much tighter socket-stall interval (20s) to avoid hanging forever on stalled HTTP/2 frames.\",[[31,36,[[null,null,null,null,1]]],[0,79,[[null,null,null,null,2]]],[132,162,[[null,null,null,null,1]]],[207,231,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]]]]],1]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[]],[null,[null,3,\"3. Why luuquangvu's Comment Misses the Architectural Bug\",[[7,17,[[null,null,null,null,3]]]]]],[null,[null,0,\"Regardless of whether a user or an internal default sets a 20s or 30s stall threshold:\"]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[[[[[null,[null,0,\"is_thinking initializes to False: When extended_thinking\\u003dTrue is requested, Gemini routinely takes 20–45+ seconds of server-side computation before flushing the first delta.\",[[0,11,[[null,null,null,null,3]]],[27,32,[[null,null,null,null,3]]],[0,33,[[null,null,null,null,2]]],[39,61,[[null,null,null,null,3]]]]]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"Because is_thinking is False at start, the watchdog cannot distinguish between an abandoned TCP connection and server-side reasoning.\",[[8,19,[[null,null,null,null,3]]],[23,28,[[null,null,null,null,3]]],[52,132,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"Even if the watchdog were 120 seconds, complex chain-of-thought prompts can hit or exceed long pauses, and any tighter watchdog or transient stall check will prematurely kill the connection.\"]]]]]]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[]],[null,[null,3,\"Suggested Reply to Set the Record Straight\"]],[null,[null,0,\"You can reply to @luuquangvu directly addressing both the default timer behavior and the state bug:\",[[17,28,[[null,null,null,null,3]]]]]]]]],null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,\"3.8 Flash\",true,[[[[1004,\"Longer\",5,null,[\"expand\",\"https://fonts.gstatic.com/s/i/short-term/release/googlesymbols/expand/default/24px.svg\",null,true]],[1005,\"Shorter\",6,null,[\"compress\",\"https://fonts.gstatic.com/s/i/short-term/release/googlesymbols/compress/default/24px.svg\",null,true]],[1003,\"Personalize\",3,null,[\"personal_recommendations\",\"https://fonts.gstatic.com/s/i/short-term/release/googlesymbols/personal_recommendations/default/24px.svg\",null,true]],[1001,\"Try again\",1,null,[\"refresh\",\"https://fonts.gstatic.com/s/i/short-term/release/googlesymbols/refresh/default/24px.svg\",null,true]]]]],null,2,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,1,1]"]]
